# Prospective audit amendment: reconstruct topology arms independently

Status: frozen before any numerical outcome. This strengthens verification only;
it does not change data, widths, leaves, hypothesis, falsifier, or resource gate.

Static review found that the first audit draft recomputed metrics from saved
sketches but trusted the producer's method labels. That would not detect a
producer that accidentally saved the same or wrongly constructed topology under
both labels. The independent audit must therefore reimplement row-stream FD and
the balanced/left-deep merge operators without importing the producer, rebuild
all three arms from the source matrix, and compare reconstructed versus saved
covariance operators, accumulated shrink mass, and shrink counts before testing
the prospective inequalities.

Because singular-vector signs are not identifiable, equality is checked through
the covariance operator. Its Frobenius difference is computed from small Gram
matrices, avoiding a dense `d x d` allocation. Timing remains producer telemetry
and is not independently reconstructed.
